Subject: [PATCH 1/3] feat: translate proposal intro/closing text and
 per-proposal summary
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three more untranslated regions found on the proposal page:

1. The H2 above the summary and the closing line before "Speak to our
   team" (introTitles/closingParagraphs) were picked at random from
   fixed English arrays in proposalCopy.ts, never wired to next-intl.
   Moved into site_copy (proposal.introTitles.0-4 /
   closingParagraphs.0-3) — only 9 fixed strings, translated once via
   the existing seed:site-copy pipeline, zero per-proposal Lara cost.
   generateProposal() now also returns the picked index so
   page.tsx can resolve it through getTranslations("proposal") instead
   of the raw English string (kept as fallback for the no-match case).

2. The dynamic summary paragraph ("Created exclusively for X adults
   for [dates], this proposal has been crafted around [experiences]...")
   is genuinely unique per proposal (buildProposalSummary.ts interpolates
   guest count/dates/experiences/moods into an English template) — not a
   fixed set, so it can't be pre-seeded like the arrays above. Translated
   on-demand in /api/translate-proposal-experiences at generation time
   (same "translate once, not per view" principle as the experience
   content) and stored in Proposal.proposal_data.summary_it, which
   page.tsx now prefers over recomputing+retranslating the English
   version on every visit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
